---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
  title="About Honest Picture"
  description="Honest Picture is an independent, research-backed library and assessment that helps people understand where they actually stand in life — using real population data and peer-reviewed studies, not advice or judgment. Here is who we are, how we work, and the standards we hold."
  path="/about"
  ogImage="/og/page--about.png"
  eyebrow="About"
  heading="A mirror made of data."
  lede="Honest Picture exists to answer one quiet, near-universal question — am I okay? — not with reassurance or alarm, but with honest context drawn from real research."
>
  <h2>Why this exists</h2>
  <p>
    Almost everyone, at some point, measures their life against a standard and
    comes up short. The standard is usually invisible and almost always wrong: a
    blend of curated social feeds, the most successful people in your particular
    circle, and a timeline you absorbed without ever checking it against reality.
  </p>
  <p>
    You see your own life from the inside — every doubt, every gap, every
    unfinished thing. You see everyone else from the outside, at their most
    composed. The result is a feeling of being behind a pace that, in the actual
    population data, frequently does not exist.
  </p>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} takes the specific facts of your life — your age, income, savings,
    time, relationships, health, and sense of direction — and places them inside
    real research and real population data. Not to tell you that you are doing well
    or badly. To show you what your situation actually looks like from the outside.
  </p>

  <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A research library</strong> of in-depth, plainly written articles —
      each answering a specific, honest question about money, time, work,
      relationships, health, purpose, comparison, regret, life stages, or happiness,
      and each grounded in cited data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The Context Assessment</strong>, a free, private tool that places your
      own answers next to population data across six areas of life. It runs entirely
      in your browser and stores nothing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A published methodology and full source list</strong>, so you can see
      exactly how the content is made and where every figure comes from.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is an independent publication and research project — not a startup
    selling a program, not a personality-quiz brand, and not affiliated with any
    company whose products it might recommend. It is written and edited by a small
    team that reads the underlying research, cross-checks the figures, and writes in
    careful, non-judgmental language. Our interest is in getting the picture right,
    not in getting you to buy anything.
  </p>

  <h2>How we make the content</h2>
  <p>
    Every insight page follows the same disciplined process, described in full on
    our <a href="/research-methodology">research methodology</a> page:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>We start from a real, specific question people actually ask.</li>
    <li>We gather figures from government statistics, large surveys, and peer-reviewed studies — never from anecdote or invention.</li>
    <li>We hedge numbers honestly ("roughly," "about," "research on this is mixed") and say so plainly when the evidence is weak or contested.</li>
    <li>We separate what the data shows, why it can feel different, what actually helps, and — just as importantly — what does not help.</li>
    <li>We cite our sources on every page and keep a full <a href="/data-sources">source list</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our editorial standards</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Trust first.</strong> If a claim is not backed by a real, citable source, it does not go on the page. We never invent statistics or studies.</li>
    <li><strong>Context, not verdicts.</strong> We show you the distribution. We do not grade your place in it or tell you that you are doing well or badly.</li>
    <li><strong>Honest about uncertainty.</strong> We distinguish strong findings from weak ones, flag where research is mixed, and note where data is thin or skewed toward particular countries.</li>
    <li><strong>Humane on hard topics.</strong> Where a subject is genuinely painful, we aim to be accurate and kind at once — never minimising a real difficulty, never inflating a common experience into a personal failing, and pointing toward qualified professionals where someone may need real help.</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy by design.</strong> The assessment runs in your browser; your answers are never stored or transmitted.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    We take accuracy seriously and we would genuinely rather hear about an error
    than not. Each page carries a "last reviewed" date, and we update figures as new
    data is published. If you spot something that looks wrong or out of date, please
    tell us on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> — include the page and, if you
    can, a source — and we will review and correct or annotate it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we are — and what we are not</h2>
  <p>
    We are a publication and a tool, built on publicly available research,
    government statistics, and peer-reviewed studies. We are not a personality quiz,
    a productivity app, a self-help brand, or a substitute for therapy or
    professional advice. Nothing here is medical, psychological, financial, or legal
    advice — see our <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a>. We do not sell a
    transformation, and we do not promise that seeing your situation clearly will
    fix it.
  </p>

  <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
  <p>
    Keeping the library free and open costs money to research, write, and host. The
    site is supported by advertising and may display ads served through Google
    AdSense. Advertising never influences our editorial content: which studies we
    cite and what we conclude are decided on the evidence alone, independently of
    any advertiser. Ads are never placed inside the assessment or its results, and
    never adjacent to a specific data finding. See our
    <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> for how advertising cookies work
    and how to opt out.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, corrections, or a source you think we should use? Email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, visit our
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, read our
    <a href="/research-methodology">research methodology</a>, or see
    <a href="/data-sources">every source we use</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
